-- title:
--   Non-norms at exactly one place are impossible (prime cyclic degree)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a finite Galois extension of $K$, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism $\tau$ of $L$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (so $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$), assume the degree $[L:K] = \operatorname{finrank}_K L$ is a prime number, and let $a$ be a unit of $K$, i.e. a nonzero element of $K$. Consider, for a height one prime $v$ of the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_K$, the image of $a$ under the canonical map $K \to K_v$ into the $v$-adic completion, and the set $S_{\mathrm{fin}}$ of those $v$ for which this image does not lie in the image of the map sending a unit $x$ of $L \otimes_K K_v$ to $\mathrm{Norm}_{K_v}(x)$; likewise, for an infinite place $w$ of $K$, let $S_\infty$ be the set of those $w$ for which the image of $a$ in the completion $K_w$ is not of the form $\mathrm{Norm}_{K_w}(x)$ for a unit $x$ of $L \otimes_K K_w$. The assertion is twofold: $S_{\mathrm{fin}}$ is finite, and the sum of the cardinalities $\#S_{\mathrm{fin}} + \#S_\infty$ (computed with `Set.ncard`) is not equal to $1$.
--
--   This is the local–global consequence of Artin reciprocity for a cyclic extension: the local norm obstructions of a global element, measured by local Artin symbols, multiply to the identity, so a single non-trivial local obstruction cannot occur. It refines the quadratic parity statement [`NumberField.finite_and_even_ncard_places_not_mem_range_norm_of_finrank_eq_two`](thm.html#NumberField.finite_and_even_ncard_places_not_mem_range_norm_of_finrank_eq_two) to cyclic extensions of prime degree, and it is used in the automorphic-form lemmas [`AutomorphicForm.exists_finset_not_isNormOf_and_not_card_eq_one_of_mem_sup_of_not_mem_range_of_prime`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_finset_not_isNormOf_and_not_card_eq_one_of_mem_sup_of_not_mem_range_of_prime) and [`AutomorphicForm.exists_finset_not_isNormOf_and_not_card_eq_one_of_ratio_not_mem_range_norm_of_prime`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_finset_not_isNormOf_and_not_card_eq_one_of_ratio_not_mem_range_norm_of_prime).
